Subject: [PATCH] Send Spout and NDI output from hidden windows that render while hidden
---
TEMPORARY: remove this patch, and its entry in portfile.cmake, once this change is in
SGCT upstream and the REF in portfile.cmake points at a commit that contains it.

`Window::draw` already renders a hidden window whose configuration sets `alwaysrender`,
but `Window::renderFBOTexture` returned early for every hidden window. That function is
where SGCT sends the window's Spout (and NDI) output, so a hidden window with a `spout`
entry never sent anything. Proposed by Marco Silva (Elumenati) as the "windowless Spout
rendering fix", 2026-09-18.
diff --git a/src/window.cpp b/src/window.cpp
index 8a78aae..2432f16 100644
--- a/src/window.cpp
+++ b/src/window.cpp
@@ -1083,7 +1083,7 @@ void Window::draw() {
 void Window::renderFBOTexture() {
     ZoneScoped;
 
-    if (!isVisible()) [[unlikely]] {
+    if (!(isVisible() || isRenderingWhileHidden())) [[unlikely]] {
         return;
     }
 
